      "message": "Logically I think this works fine but it reads a bit funny as typically you have `result \u003d value \u0026 ~mask;`. Also, this leaves the `fpscr` variable with the pre-masked value. Rewriting to the following would read a bit easier and ensure the `fpscr` variable is consistent with the `fpscr` register after clearing.\n\n```suggestion\nstatic void clear_fpscr(void)\n{\n\tfpscr \u003d  _read_fpscr() \u0026 ~FPU_FPSCR_EXC_FLAGS;\n\tasm volatile(\"vmsr fpscr, %0\" : : \"r\"(fpscr));\n}\n```",
